[[rust-vterm]]
documents: support/test_writing/rust/README.txt, support/test_writing/python/README-hwut_vterm.txt
'Screen' and 'Terminal' in Rust read libvterm's screen, cells and events through dlopen -- no header, no crate -- as 'hwut_vterm.py' does through ctypes, run an application on a pseudo-terminal it cannot tell from a person's, and name a missing library alike: held against the Python test's GOOD files by link.
README.txt, sections 2, 3; ../python/README-hwut_vterm.txt.

[[go-random]]
documents: support/test_writing/go/README.txt
'DeterministicStream' and 'SelectionMarker' in Go draw the stream 'deterministic_random.py' draws, seed for seed: the Go test prints the Python test's GOOD files byte for byte -- 'gauss' within the band its GOOD allows the libm path -- which it is held against by link.
README.txt, section 2; deterministicrandom/deterministic_random.go.

[[go-timeline]]
documents: support/test_writing/go/README.txt
'TriggerDispatcher' in Go fires, orders and announces as 'deterministic_timeline.py' does, and its run -- a task on an event loop of asyncio's order -- interleaves with a consumer and is cancelled as an asyncio task is: held against the Python test's GOOD files by link.
README.txt, section 2; deterministictimeline/deterministic_timeline.go.

[[go-space]]
documents: support/test_writing/go/README.txt
